 :selected-path
 {:identity "Only Axxium axx_ agent credentials on the pinned identity lineage. Exclude browser/JWT sessions, operator authentication via agent secret, service-admin bypass, and other identity issuers from v1. Axxium remains the sole actor/credential validity authority; Emacs is resource consent issuer, not an identity system."
  :identity-extension "Extend the actual active-credential lookup to return, to a trusted fixed host bridge only, actor ID, entity ID, credential ID, credential expiry and an owner-managed nonreused credential/actor invalidation generation. Current actor-only lookup cannot distinguish two credentials for one actor. Generation must be derived from Axxium-owned durable lifecycle state under its transaction protocol; never hash a bearer token or invent it in Sol/Emacs. Axxium issuance/revocation and all actor-disable/delete/credential-expiry paths applicable to this flow must participate in a reviewed fence protocol. No applicable path may bypass it, including administrative DB access; if the operational trust boundary cannot ensure that, deny. Session deletion is excluded with JWT sessions, not silently claimed covered."
  :operator "Owner's local, human-authenticated operator control must independently approve the exact presented immutable request and resource. Authentication and capture of operator approval are not implemented by the inspected source; a synthetic approval exercises only shape/state. No model or remote tool may impersonate the human."
  :sol "Optional fixed transport of closed data and opaque handles; not an issuer, identity source or policy decision. Prefer no Sol code until an actual carrier is selected and reviewed."
  :govone "Independent read disclosure policy owner; no GovOne decision grants buffer ownership or consent. Existing Decision and bundle version do not deliver the required destination-bound ordering. Read release stays denied until real owner-qualified integration exists. Writes do not thereby gain policy or resource authority."
  :scope "Only fresh synthetic agent-owned direct buffers, subject to actual direct-object and lifetime exclusion proof. No existing private buffers, general evaluator, shell, arbitrary commands, raw IPC, or i3 effects."}
 :closed-shapes
 {:notation "Maps below are exact required keys; no optional or unknown keys unless explicitly written. Strings are Unicode scalar UTF-8 without normalization; identifiers are constrained ASCII as defined. Buffers and byte arrays shown in types are owner-held values, not serialized host objects. Versions are literal ASCII. All records are immutable copied values; duplicate keys, noncanonical encoding, metadata, invalid scalars, out-of-bounds integers and trailing bytes deny before any effect."
  :types {:uuid "canonical lowercase RFC4122 UUID text, 36 ASCII bytes"
          :id "1..128 ASCII bytes from [A-Za-z0-9._:-], owner-generated or Axxium-returned"
          :digest "32 raw bytes SHA-256"
          :u64 "integer 0..9007199254740991"
          :instant "u64 milliseconds since Unix epoch"
          :nonce "32 bytes from an owner-approved CSPRNG; opaque and secret where used as a capability reference"
          :bytes "0..4096 raw bytes; UTF-8 scalar sequence when text"
          :opaque-handle "owner-custodied 32-byte random reference plus authenticated channel binding; reference alone is never authority"}
  :identity-proof {:shape "{:v 's4a.identity/v1', :actor-id id, :entity-id id, :credential-id id, :actor-generation u64, :credential-generation u64, :credential-not-after instant, :channel-binding digest, :owner-epoch uuid}"
                   :provenance "Produced inside the Axxium-owned verified agent-credential path and conveyed only by an authenticated integrity-protected fixed bridge bound to its peer/channel. Existing source only returns actor/entity; credential ID, expiry, generations and bridge are missing extensions. Claims from the request, tool output, Sol or a caller are never this proof. No bearer, token hash or credential secret appears in a grant or log."
                   :validity "Proof must be bound to an identity-owner fence ticket whose invalidation ordering is established below; signed bytes or lookup freshness alone do not qualify."}
  :resource "{:owner-epoch uuid, :incarnation uuid, :revision u64, :bytes u64}; all derived by the Emacs owner from a live registered direct buffer object; bytes <= 1048576. Object handle is privately stored, not client-resolved by name. Fresh epoch on each owner start."
  :invocation {:read "{:v 's4a.invocation/v1', :op 'emacs/read-range', :actor-id id, :entity-id id, :credential-id id, :actor-generation u64, :credential-generation u64, :channel-binding digest, :resource resource, :start u64, :end u64, :destination-id id, :contract-digest digest}"
               :replace "{:v 's4a.invocation/v1', :op 'emacs/replace-range', :actor-id id, :entity-id id, :credential-id id, :actor-generation u64, :credential-generation u64, :channel-binding digest, :resource resource, :start u64, :end u64, :replacement bytes, :contract-digest digest}"
               :rules "Owner constructs identity fields from the trusted proof and resource fields from its own registry, never copies authority from the requester. 0 <= start <= end <= resource bytes, end-start <= 4096, UTF-8 character boundaries, resulting buffer <= 1048576. Read destination identifies one owner-configured first trusted custody endpoint, not a URL or client-selectable arbitrary recipient. Replace contains literal UTF-8 bytes only. Contract digest is exact approved Oikos v1 contract digest; this envelope is separate from and must not silently alter the frozen Oikos request schema."}
  :canonical {:encoding "Owner binding bytes are a fixed binary transcript, not a generic EDN/JSON printer: ASCII magic S4A-OWNER followed by byte 0x01; each field encoded in the exact order listed below. A text or byte field is unsigned 32-bit big-endian byte length then exact bytes; u64 is eight unsigned big-endian bytes constrained to safe range; uuid is length-prefixed canonical ASCII; digest is exactly 32 bytes; no maps or key strings on wire."
              :order ["v" "op" "actor-id" "entity-id" "credential-id" "actor-generation" "credential-generation" "channel-binding" "resource.owner-epoch" "resource.incarnation" "resource.revision" "resource.bytes" "start" "end" "read:destination-id OR replace:replacement" "contract-digest"]
              :binding "SHA-256 of the entire transcript is the compact binding; retain the exact immutable transcript privately and compare both digest and byte equality at issue and final execution. Unknown versions, alternate encodings, extra data or changed bytes deny. Independently authored cross-language golden vectors required before acceptance; no assertion this encoding matches the separately reviewed 550-byte dispatcher vector."}
  :operator-approval {:shape "{:v 's4a.approval/v1', :approval-id uuid, :operator-id id, :owner-epoch uuid, :invocation-digest digest, :issued-at instant, :not-after instant, :scope 'emacs/read'|'emacs/write'}"
                      :provenance "Owner creates after verified human approval of exact immutable invocation and scope, with the approval bound to exact transcript and operator session. Scope must match operation; IDs/time come from owner, not client. UI/authentication are missing, no unauthenticated interactive command is presumed safe."
                      :custody "An approval record is private owner state, not an externally assertable approval map. Read requires owner resource grant separately from GovOne; replace requires explicit approval for that exact replacement."}
  :grant {:shape "{:v 's4a.grant/v1', :grant-id uuid, :approval-id uuid, :owner-epoch uuid, :invocation-digest digest, :issued-at instant, :not-after instant, :state 'issued'|'consumed'|'revoked'|'invalidated'}"
          :provenance "Owner derives from an approved immutable transcript, exact owner registration and one authenticated proof. Store owner-held opaque grant reference separately; neither UUID nor hash is an authorization token. Persist tombstones through the qualified existing owner storage adapter; storage is not identified or qualified yet."
          :transitions "Only absent->issued after approval; issued->consumed or issued->revoked in owner serialization order. consumed and revoked terminal; issued->invalidated on expiry, restart, epoch loss or identity/policy invalidation. No terminal->issued or reuse. consumed before effect remains consumed even if later denied or indeterminate. Revocation of consumed reports already-consumed, not a false pre-effect guarantee."}
  :revocation {:request "{:v 's4a.revoke/v1', :owner-epoch uuid, :grant-id uuid, :operator-id id, :reason-code 'operator-revoked'}; operator-id comes from authenticated owner control, never request authority."
               :result "Exactly one of {:v 's4a.revoke-result/v1', :status 'revoked', :grant-id uuid, :owner-order u64}, {:v 's4a.revoke-result/v1', :status 'already-revoked', :grant-id uuid, :owner-order u64}, {:v 's4a.revoke-result/v1', :status 'already-consumed', :grant-id uuid}, or {:v 's4a.revoke-result/v1', :status 'unavailable'}. No raw errors."
               :ack "Only revoked/already-revoked after durable tombstone and serialization is a consent-revoke ACK. If mutation was already ordered first, revoke cannot undo it. Failure/uncertain persistence is unavailable, never a successful ACK. Axxium and GovOne acknowledgements are separate and must not be relabeled."}
  :release-decision {:shape "{:v 's4a.release/v1', :decision-id uuid, :invocation-digest digest, :actor-id id, :credential-id id, :destination-id id, :owner-epoch uuid, :policy-scope-id id, :policy-generation u64, :issued-at instant, :not-after instant, :effect 'allow'}"
                     :provenance "A proposed trusted GovOne-owner integration must create and retain this bound decision plus a policy-owner fence ticket; it is not the shape or result of current GovOne Evaluate. No client, Sol, operator approval or mutable bundle-version string may mint it. Denial, missing fields, unqualified destination, expired ticket or unverifiable custody releases zero bytes. If this new integration cannot be qualified, read release remains held."
                     :first-custody "For this protocol, first release is the first transfer of plaintext beyond the Emacs owner into the one authenticated destination endpoint whose immutable identity is bound above. A return value, queue, socket write or callback receiving plaintext counts as release if outside owner custody. Capturing content in an owner-private local buffer is not release. No plaintext may enter an unqualified queue or log; any subsequent egress requires its own GovOne-governed boundary."}}
 :time
 {:trusted-source "A qualified owner time adapter combines an OS monotonic clock with a trusted UTC time measurement, both obtained in-process from the owner host. Maximum permitted absolute UTC uncertainty is 1000 ms, including measurement age/drift; it must be demonstrated, not inferred from wall-clock precision. No qualified adapter is established in inspected source. Failure to bound uncertainty, unavailable readings, monotonic regression, detected wall-clock rollback or clock discontinuity invalidates in-flight grants and denies."
  :issuance "At issuance obtain [earliest,latest] UTC bounds; issued-at is latest; not-after is min(operator requested deadline, latest+60000ms, credential-not-after, any applicable policy not-after). Reject unless earliest <= latest and latest < not-after. Also derive an owner-epoch monotonic deadline conservatively from not-after minus latest; never extend it on wall-clock corrections. Exact policy/identity bounds must come from their owners, not caller data."
  :final-check "After every potentially blocking identity/policy/storage action and immediately before the first mutation instruction or first plaintext transfer, take a fresh bounded clock reading; require latest < each approval, grant, credential and, for reads, governance deadline, and monotonic now strictly less than epoch deadline. Equality denies. Between that check and linearization no yielding, callback, I/O, or independently mutable authority may intervene; inability to prove this holds the operation. A grant consumed while fresh but expired during durable consume remains consumed and causes zero mutation/release."
  :restart "Restart, process epoch change or lost clock continuity invalidates all old proof, approval, grants and handles, regardless of persisted timestamps. Durable tombstones must still recover before new admissions; no old grant is reactivated."}
 :atomic-owner-protocol
 {:required-exclusion "Actual owner implementation must prove every buffer mutation, alias creation and destruction, reentrancy, grant issuance/revocation, and relevant admission or release runs in one finite serialized owner domain. Prove direct buffer identity, widened byte facts, no indirect/shared-text aliases throughout, and reject hooks, overlays and unsupported paths. A mutex guarding only oikos-native--operate and a callback returning true do not fence other Emacs actions. If Emacs cannot enforce this for a fixture, no effect is admitted."
  :distributed-order "Axxium credential/actor invalidations and GovOne policy updates cannot be ordered by an Emacs lock alone. Required future integration must define fixed authenticated fence tickets that either hold the respective owner serialization rights across final Emacs linearization or provide an equivalent proved protocol: invalidation cannot acknowledge its capability-effective change ahead of a still-valid conflicting ticket, and disconnect, crash or lease uncertainty fails closed. All invalidation/update paths and recovery must participate. Existing Axxium revoke 200 and GovOne Evaluate/BundleVersion do not satisfy this. There is no claim that the proposed ticket or a safe distributed lock already exists; if ownership/failure proofs are unavailable, hold."
  :write-sequence ["Authenticate and bind Axxium credential under a qualified ticket; resolve owner object and closed invocation; obtain owner human approval and exact single-use grant."
                   "Enter the proven common owner serialization boundary; check grant is issued, exact bytes and object/facts match, operator scope valid and identity ticket valid."
                   "Durably transition issued->consumed before any mutation using a proven single-writer, crash-consistent owner storage adapter; failures deny and uncertain commit is indeterminate. No process-memory table is durable proof."
                   "After storage completes, recheck all relevant identity, consent, exclusivity, facts, bounds and trusted time without a gap before native effect. If expired/revoked/uncertain, perform zero mutation and retain consumed."
                   "Linearization is the first native text-changing instruction on that exact buffer inside the exclusion boundary. Current delete-region then insert is two operations and can partially fail; it is not all-or-nothing. After possible start, failure or lost reply is indeterminate; do not retry."]
  :read-sequence ["Resolve the exact read invocation and obtain separate owner read grant plus GovOne destination-bound qualified release decision and tickets. No private content leaves owner custody before release."
                  "Under the same proven exclusion/order, check exact resource, grant, Axxium ticket and governance ticket; bounded read and any required durable consumption occur privately. After blocking steps recheck time and all current facts."
                  "Linearization is the actual first plaintext transfer to the bound authenticated destination; the decision check and transfer must be indivisible against relevant revokes/policy updates. If the destination transport requires a blocking or yieldable send outside the fence, no release until an equivalent owner-governed custody transfer is proved."]
  :revoke "A revoke enters the same owner order, durably persists the terminal tombstone, then sends ACK. A revoke ACK before write linearization or first release guarantees no effect/release for the revoked grant; a concurrent operation has a recorded total order; after completion cannot undo. A durable consume ordered before revoke does not itself prove mutation happened."
  :durability "The selected storage must be an existing owner-approved Clio/Receipt River adapter only if independently demonstrated to provide atomic durable commit, exclusive writer fencing, complete recovery and rollback detection in this actual deployment. No such adapter is established. Append-only data, fsync assertions, unique random IDs or a process mutex alone do not prove these properties. If unavailable, deny rather than create a new ledger/kernel. Under proved guarantees, at most one admitted attempt per grant; never promise exactly-once effects or recovery of an unobserved result."
  :failure "No automatic retry after consume or any possibly started effect; lost response or partial mutation is indeterminate. An ACK of owner-consent revocation is not an Axxium revocation ACK or a GovOne policy-update ACK. Disconnect and incomplete recovery fail closed."}
